# A form can be `reduce`'s structure without parentheses, even before an
# `init:` clause. Subtle: the inner lambda's body stops at `init`, so this
# reads `reduce (map xs with f) init: 0 with g`.
#= {result: 6, inputs: {xs: [1, 2]}}
reduce map xs with fn x -> x * 2 init: 0 with fn acc, x -> acc + x
